{"kind":"report","text":"Completed narrow static settlement-accounting review at exact 479987f6cb34d6aaf0d23d309c6d059f536f9b48, direct parent 3ed99af50e645d68c1885e5ef612b98a7e160588. This completes only checker promise 6365c41d under request 51baeefc. The original three-hold reserve witness in 1f52493c closes, but this is not complete capacity assurance.\n\nThe prospective third hold would leave ten written entries and four owed against twelve. turn.ts 267–272 throws Full after sealing/folding; 240–246 catches it outside the SQLite transaction. The attempted entry, fold, outbox, retained inputs and accepted-key record roll back, and scope-full names original head 8. The two admitted ends fit at entries 9–10 and a checkpoint at 11. No unexplained reserve number was raised; settlementReserve is removed. Simple unresolved request/diagnosis/result and outside-attempt unknown/final counts match current fold shapes, as does provisional confirmation. The changed compact witness is meaningful by static reading only.\n\nTwo boundaries stay within the existing full-capacity owner/request 1f52493c, not a duplicate commission.\n\n1. Checkpoint accounting does not preserve the literal 'written plus owed' invariant. reserve.ts 36 always counts one checkpoint, but fits 59 subtracts it for every checkpoint without changing that folded obligation. At scopeEntries 6, founding plus offer/assign/take-hold gives head 3, four used and two owed. Intermediate checkpoint 4 fits as five + two - one = six. Its poststate nevertheless has five used and two still counted as owed. Hold-end 5 then fills six, and core's absolute cap refuses a checkpoint through the final expiry. This is a concrete count/wording boundary. Adopted R1 revision7 section9.2 reserves checkpoint capacity but does not explicitly require a final closing checkpoint; do not infer a new adopted requirement. Newly filed R1 revision9 explicitly proposes one closing checkpoint and treats other checkpoints as new work (main4623,4701–4702). Under that proposed policy intermediate checkpoints must preserve the closing slot, or folded state must explicitly identify when the counted duty is consumed/rearmed. The present blanket subtraction cannot demonstrate 'one checkpoint always' and the post-fold guarantee stated in the delta note. R4/I1/R1 must settle that policy together before certifying the complete repair.\n\n2. Result clauses can rearm one timed rule even when the timed-only graph is acyclic. Supported existing grammar: a ticket request type with live asked and paused states and optional mutable until; ask sets until from the clock plus60 and sends two tells; both applied clauses set asked; one timed rule on asked changes it to paused, with no attention. With eight entries, genesis0 and ask1 fit: four request entries, one timer and one checkpoint are owed, totaling eight. A finite allowed trace is timer2; delivery-unavailable diagnosis A3; late authentic result A4 rearms asked; timer5; diagnosis B6; result B7 rearms asked; timer8 then hits the absolute ceiling. Existing validator432–435,540–566,690–707 admits these forms; there is no final-item mutation or timed-rule cycle. reserve57–58 exempts both diagnoses/results from fits, while the count's one-per-rule-per-live-item does not cover those revisits. This is a supported source/composition accounting seam, not a claim that the current submit-only scope interface already executes deliveries. Its transport remains step4 work. Reserve the finite closure of mandatory follow-on duties or reject unsupported definitions/configurations at admission; merely disclosing timed cycles does not address this acyclic witness.\n\nThe delta note correctly disclaims bytes, outbox row count, second creation results/conflicts, timed cycles and cost. These are remaining complete I1/R1/R4 duties, not permission to abandon already admitted work. Byte-size timed totality and sealed-receipt precedence remain under e312b380. The later3ed early no-item retention repair remains intact. Historical scans are also disclosed: the SQLite request aggregate includes undelivered rows with no result, and MemoryState scans historical requests/attempts; repeated replay/admission accounting can accumulate substantial work. No bounded global update cost or measured10x saving follows. The cover map survives an abandoned founding transaction, but no surviving scope uses it and a successful founding replaces it; no wrong admission is demonstrated, only a small qualification of 'nothing kept in memory'.\n\nRead provenance: root read the complete36,691-character eleven-path diff through EOF, complete new reserve.ts and relevant actual fresh contexts; full prior4b/3ed source reading transferred through complete changes. Independent lifecycle audit read every changed byte of all eleven paths, complete settle/timed and relevant fold/clause/validator/fixture contexts. Independent storage audit reread full current reserve60,state275,SQLite237,core285,turn326LF, complete delta section15 and affected fixture/witness context. Current byte/LF/SHA-256 ledger: delta53006/342/e82c4d4beac8cf5fc265848bc0f26822da60045a394c6f822827b816a87d6350; bounds3009/80/60850621503dcd2983e6d133c8f323301533ebd93d1bb1031978f2afc097b583; deriveREADME12690/164/532f9dff35c6896892f48e0b6dee60511c001652ed847b76f767391bfe8819b1; deriveindex495/17/fbe54e087b7ef49f755ca3c9070f9b41670f104c02b24d576bb058c8c64acfad; reserve3108/60/08c5128a0d0af59db55d4f4ece2894bbfa029621037111ebdeb3b1cb807efc5c; state14557/275/59df03483c2c093a739335eadbfbd50b0296a80aee15380fbcd936e4fae638d4; scopeREADME7682/123/78be8396696650fdfe2712e88f656c688dd9c96be25d7257276d84050444a2fc; core16359/285/271ff714ccdf7f7c4184c3eaeeec6d9d0ab7ca01c941a06aa07f2e419572e870; SQLite16222/237/e4e0a32cae1510f9b1799fe9bd502c4ff49863f4472550faba3b55fd098a31fb; turn16641/327/bdb6d387fd17bde69c952b54f447fb54254eace8a8991cbace684106f1a242c6; turntests11258/164/d726b52ba5850dd2138a3b7071116d944d7fb498871c1fa0c845f7c6ba738099.\n\nNo test/project/build/install/typecheck/private diagnostic execution, source edit or provider effect. Producer test evidence is not checker verification. All choices remain proposed; current R1 revision9 has its own accepted ordinary review e027f00c. Complete source/transport/service bindings/authority/independent replay/client/removal and application/cloud/browser/device/operator/unknown-effect duties stay owed. This is a narrow static repair report, not final ordinary I1 approval or complete-dimensional-capacity certification.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6365c41dccd5edcfc4e6a808b6d4d207c1004b08 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4e7b67b62fc517a84878ddda441f99d1f98872dc, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dc24e2e1fade3048eece3d431345c013dc80de8e"}}